board_guidance.risk_appetite:
4.5 of 5, easing toward 4. Net debt has been $0.0B since 2029 and holds in base and stress in every Do Nothing column, but our record shows no cash returned and no later rating. Our limits are unchanged:
- -$1B per Board item in any of S1-S3;
- the plan's S3 no lower than -2.83;
- a launch must show more than +$1B in the expected column;
- one development at a time;
- a premium cap of $2B.

would_approve:
A 10-year Solo fps, in a round whose grid supports it. That means:
- an item value above +$1B in the expected column;
- no lower than -$1B in every plausible column;
- S3 no lower than $2B below Do Nothing;
- stress net debt held;
- Pope's results clean.
The engine code rides with it. This round the best 10-year falls short: -1.78 at Renton, which is $2.78B below the business-case bar and $0.78-0.88B past the Downside limit. The 10-year still beats the 7-year by $1.21-1.53B in every column and has the higher worst column (-2.94 at Renton against -4.15), so it remains our preferred ramp.

would_veto:
fps: launch_7yr. Its item value against hold is -2.99 to -3.36, and -3.43 to -3.81 with the Re-engine. It fails three tests:
- Business case;
- Downside;
- Rating first: S3 runs -3.68 to -4.19 against -2.83, short by $0.85-1.36B.
Stress net debt is not held ($0.5-4.7B), so it also fails the Fundable gate (advice). Paired with a 2045 Re-engine, the two developments overlap 5 years, which fails One development at a time. It trails the 10-year by $1.21-1.53B in every column. Acceptable alternative: hold.

recommendations.text:
The fps is closer but not there. Against hold, the 10-year at Renton has moved from about -4.3 in 2035 to -1.78 now. Prepare, but do not announce, the 2050 case: the 10-year ramp at Renton, with Pope's wind-down plan. Show three things beside each fps row:
- the Do Nothing erosion (preference 27.7% in 2050 and 16.0% in 2060; profit $1.43B a year below the game baseline by 2060);
- the value of waiting to 2050;
- the trend of the item value since 2030.
2050 is the last round, and we will judge it on that round's grid alone. Give no fps date before launch, and set a conservative EIS, with room built in, at launch.

