recommendations.text:
Add three items to the full Board's twice-yearly safety review:
- NGSA at about 100 a month, with three engine makers (CFM, plus the P&W and Rolls-Royce Joint Venture engine);
- the closure of the last A320 lines (28 aircraft in 2045, none from 2047), with skills and quality kept on the fewest lines to the end;
- any Re-engine development running alongside.
A quality escape, a safety event or an engine supply crunch comes back to the Board.

levers_in_play:
Other moves the board does not price:
- own-ramp supply agreements;
- recruitment sized to our own needs;
- zero-for-zero trade advocacy;
- the internal A350 case paper.
The brief lists no cancel option this round.

