red_lines:
Override budget: one per game, still unused. An override needs:
- at least $1B over the best passing option;
- a record as a Board item;
- on a Qualified Majority item, a lead in the worst plausible column too.
The Re-engine's +0.89 cannot carry one, and the Board vetoes a Re-engine that comes through an override.

Cash and balance sheet [AX-0104, AX-0022, AX-0102, A-0401]:
- programme spend at most $5.2B a year;
- net cash and the A+/A1 rating protected;
- payout within 30-50%, and buybacks within the AGM authority;
- no equity raise; state support counts as upside only.

Disclosure [AX-0004, AX-0005]:
- windows, not dates;
- no internal long-term-plan targets and no payout figures;
- no Delay Tactics;
